sec.p:
Twenty (36%) studies received a “strong” methodological quality rating, while 36 (64%) were rated as “adequate” (see Appendix Table 5 and 6). Overall, the studies eligible for this review described the participants, the intervention, and the outcome measures in detail, conducted data analyses that fit the research questions, and provided information about generalization or maintenance of the targeted behaviors, thus making replications possible. Table 3
